            <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); letter-spacing: -0.03em;">Healthcare SEO</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed mb-4 fade-up stagger-child" style="--i:1;">Queen Elizabeth Hospital, Birmingham Children's Hospital, multiple NHS trusts, private clinics, dental practices, and specialist providers across the city. Healthcare SEO faces the tightest YMYL requirements of any sector. Google does not compromise here.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed mb-4 fade-up stagger-child" style="--i:2;">Google's quality raters require healthcare content authored by qualified medical professionals, citing peer-reviewed sources, making no unsupported claims. Content that fails these standards gets suppressed regardless of how good the technical SEO is.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed fade-up stagger-child" style="--i:3;">We build healthcare strategies that satisfy YMYL while still driving patient enquiries and bookings. Author bio schema linked to professional registrations. Content review processes. Local SEO for practice visibility. Conversion optimisation that respects the sensitivity of healthcare decisions. For private practices competing with NHS services in search, positioning and content differentiation are critical.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-4 fade-up stagger-child" style="--i:4;">
          <div class="border border-zinc-800 p-5">
