          </div>
          <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4 fade-up stagger-child" style="--i:1;">The Bullring and Grand Central pull over 36 million visitors a year. Beyond these anchors, Birmingham sustains a vibrant independent retail scene across the Jewellery Quarter, Digbeth, and suburban high streets. The hospitality sector — led by the Balti Triangle, Brindleyplace, and a growing fine dining scene — runs hot.</p>
          <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4 fade-up stagger-child" style="--i:2;">Retail SEO splits between e-commerce (product pages, Shopping feeds, category optimisation) and local SEO (Google Business Profile, maps, reviews, footfall queries). For hospitality, local SEO dominates. Profile completeness, review velocity, and menu/booking structured data are the main ranking factors.</p>
          <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed fade-up stagger-child" style="--i:3;">We tailor to the operating model. Pure e-commerce gets product schema, Shopping feed optimisation, and category content. Brick-and-mortar gets citation building and Profile management. Restaurants and bars get review strategy, event schema, and local content targeting cuisine and occasion queries. Our <a href="/areas/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light font-bold transition-colors">area coverage</a> page details location-specific approaches.</p>
